(6849521, 1030612, 27133, '<td valign="top">Lizzie Borden took an axe,<br/>And gave her mother forty whacks.<br/>And when she saw what she had done,<br/>She gave her father forty-one.<br/> <br/>Many know that this popular childrens jump-rope rhyme refers to the infamous hatchet murders that took place in Fall River, Massachusetts on August 4, 1892, allegedly at the hands of New England spinster Lizzie Borden  (who many believe killed her father and stepmother).</td>', 'Lizzie Borden took an axe,And gave her mother forty whacks.And when she saw what she had done,She gave her father forty-one. Many know that this popular childrens jump-rope rhyme refers to the infamous hatchet murders that took place in Fall River, Massachusetts on August 4, 1892, allegedly at the hands of New England spinster Lizzie Borden  (who many believe killed her father and stepmother).', '2012-08-27 00:09:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6849523, 1030771, 138630, '<td valign="top">The maid was in the garden hanging out the clothes,<br/>When down came a blackbird and pecked off her nose!<br/> <br/>Terrific idea, well set up and I like that the processing pushes it a bit but not too much.  What a homely maid!  Voted earlier.</td>', 'The maid was in the garden hanging out the clothes,When down came a blackbird and pecked off her nose! Terrific idea, well set up and I like that the processing pushes it a bit but not too much.  What a homely maid!  Voted earlier.', '2012-08-27 00:10:48.000000', NULL, 1),
